From c24f02382df04f72a75a9097e2284d1ceb844ed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:31:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] refactor(art): drop the availability table and let
 Chinese art follow the interface language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The final state of the card-art series, on top of the commits that built it.

**The availability table is gone.** The rewrite to the CDN is unconditional and
keeps the printing id it was handed, so nothing chooses a printing and there is
nothing to look up: `images.mtgch.com` answers 404 for printings it has no art for
and the existing rung ladder falls to that CDN's English mirror. Removed with it:
`gen-derived-art-availability.sh`, its two Python helpers, the
`__SCRYFALL_IMAGES_AVAILABILITY_URL_TEMPLATE__` define, and the generated sidecar.

**Chinese card art now follows the INTERFACE language.** `artLanguage` goes back to
`"auto"`, and `zhs` joins `SUPPORTED_LNGS` so a player can actually choose Chinese.
Every browser `zh*` tag normalizes to it — the app serves ONE Chinese, simplified,
so traditional tags map there too rather than falling back.

Pinning the ART preference to Chinese was reaching the same goal the hard way: it
produced two independent Chinese switches that had to agree, plus a persistence
helper whose only job was stopping an old preferences blob from reverting one of
them. Following the interface needs neither, and it is what `"auto"` has always
meant.

The `zhs` catalogs mirror English for now — translation is deferred — but they
exist and carry en's exact key set, because i18next needs a namespace to resolve
and the locale-parity gate compares key sets. Placeholders keep that gate honest
instead of exempting the new locale from it.

Also carries the two fixes for defects the series had been shipping:
`resolvePrintingFallback` was deleted along with the availability block while its
call site remained (every placeholder-image card threw), and this rebuild strips
the card-TEXT series' fragments that had leaked into the shared files
(`preferencesStore`, `PreferencesModal`, the `settings.json` catalogs), which is
what made the series unreapplicable.
